      <h2>Story angles</h2>
      <p>Looking for a story angle? Here are 5 angles we have data and expertise to support:</p>

      <p><strong>Angle 1: The state of AI tools in 2026.</strong> We track 30+ AI tools across 24 categories. We have 2,500+ hours of hands-on testing data in 2026 alone. Story potential: the trends, the leaders, the laggards, the surprising winners.</p>

      <p><strong>Angle 2: How small teams use AI to compete.</strong> Our case studies (a 12-person engineering team, a 3-person editorial team, an 8-person marketing team) show how small teams use AI to 2-3x output. Story potential: the playbook, the tools, the ROI.</p>

      <p><strong>Angle 3: The AI agent era.</strong> AI agents are the dominant paradigm in 2026. We have reviewed every major agent platform. Story potential: what works, what does not, who is winning, what it means for knowledge work.</p>

      <p><strong>Angle 4: AI tool consolidation.</strong> 30+ tools in 24 categories is overwhelming. Our analysis: the 12 tools that cover 95% of use cases. Story potential: the curated short list, the decision framework.</p>

      <p><strong>Angle 5: AI content quality.</strong> AI slop is a real problem. We have editorial standards for AI-assisted content. Story potential: how to identify quality, how to use AI well, the standards we hold ourselves to.</p>

